  "description": "A six-week, thirty-seven-lesson path from \"I can write a SELECT\" to \"I can diagnose a production incident on a Microsoft-stack cloud platform at 2am.\"\n\nThis course is built around the tools a **cloud support engineer** actually touches: SQL Server and T-SQL through SSMS and Azure Data Studio, Python as a diagnostic instrument rather than an application language, JSON Schema as an API contract, Git as a team workflow, CI/CD pipelines, structured logging and observability, and both AWS and Azure — including Azure AD / Entra ID.\n\nEvery chapter ends with a test, and the course ends with a final exam. Two portfolio projects are built along the way.",
